Quick AI Tools - Private Client-Side Browser Utilities
Quick AI Tools is a lightweight, zero-backend, client-side web application for processing PDFs, compressing images, running local OCR text extraction, and converting document formats inside browser memory.
Features & Tools Included
Merge PDF (pdf-merge): Combine multiple PDF documents into a single file.
Split PDF (pdf-split): Extract page numbers or custom page ranges into a separate PDF file.
Rotate PDF (pdf-rotate): Permanently rotate PDF pages by 90°, 180°, or 270°.
Add Watermark (pdf-watermark): Overlay customizable text watermarks across PDF pages.
Add Page Numbers (pdf-pagenumbers): Automatically format and append page numbers to the bottom of PDF pages.
PDF to JPG (pdf-to-jpg): Render PDF pages into JPG images (downloaded directly or bundled into a ZIP archive).
Image to PDF (image-to-pdf): Convert JPG, PNG, or WebP images into a styled PDF.
Compress Image (image-compress): Re-encode canvas pixels into JPEG format with selectable quality percentages.
OCR / Text Extractor (ocr-extractor): Extract readable text from scanned images and PDFs using client-side Tesseract WebAssembly.
Word (DOCX) to Text (docx-to-txt): Extract raw document text from Word files via Mammoth.js.
Text / MD to PDF (txt-to-pdf): Convert plain text or Markdown into PDF with automatic word wrapping and page breaks.
PDF to Text (pdf-to-text): Extract readable text streams from PDF files into .txt.
How to Run Locally
Clone or download this repository.
Open index.html in any modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge).
No build step, Node.js server, or npm setup is required.
How to Deploy to GitHub Pages
Push all project files (index.html, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, README.md) to a public GitHub repository.
In your GitHub repository, navigate to Settings -> Pages.
Under Build and deployment -> Source, select Deploy from a branch.
Choose the main or master branch and set the folder to / (root). Click Save.
Update sitemap.xml and robots.txt with your actual published GitHub Pages URL (https://<username>.github.io/<repository-name>/).
Tech Stack & Open-Source Libraries
Frontend Styling: Tailwind CSS, FontAwesome 6
PDF Generation & Manipulation: PDF-Lib
PDF Rendering & Text Stream Parsing: PDF.js
Archiving / ZIP Creation: JSZip
OCR Engine: Tesseract.js
Word DOCX Parsing: Mammoth.js
Limitations & Disclosures
Browser Memory Limits: Very large files (e.g. PDFs over 100MB or multi-gigabyte images) may hit memory limitations in browser environments.
Client Processing Disclosure: Files process locally in your device memory; zero files are uploaded to remote servers.
